{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"earthen-wheat-chick","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`docs/api-stability.md:24,41-46` defines underscore-prefixed modules/functions as private, while ADR 0083 already requires one canonical binding for reconciler moves. Contrary decisions remain: ADR 0016 retains `run_security_detectors`, ADR 0092 retains reconcile compatibility, and past split documentation retained private shims to avoid consumer migration.\n\n## Approach\n\nComplete the prescribed ADR lifecycle. In RESEARCH, catalog the cited contrary decisions and write a numbered critique covering public-versus-private boundaries, dynamic/monkeypatch consumers, persisted/wire exceptions, and enforcement. Record maintainer resolution for every critique item. Then DRAFT, HOLD for review, and MERGE an ADR that mandates one canonical private binding and atomic consumer migration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- new ADR allocated through `docs/adr/.numbers`\n- `docs/api-stability.md` and architecture/reuse guidance\n- enforcement/review guidance or a mechanical guard identified by the ADR\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd a policy/documentation check or deterministic enforcement test specified by the ADR; verify existing public facade, wire-schema, and persisted-event contract tests remain unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] RESEARCH contains a numbered critique of ADR 0016, ADR 0083, ADR 0092, and prior split-shim guidance; each item has a recorded maintainer resolution.\n- [ ] The merged ADR defines one canonical binding after private moves and atomic source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch migration.\n- [ ] The ADR distinguishes valid public facades, MCP wire schemas, event readers, and persisted-data migrations from internal-only shims.\n- [ ] The ADR requires a durable review or mechanical recurrence-prevention mechanism and names its evidence.\n- [ ] The policy check/enforcement evidence passes without breaking the preserved public/wire/event contracts.","id":"8eff-87c1-d09a-4893","parent_id":"6640-ac11-5c55-46b5","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","adr","architecture","internal-shims"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: prohibit internal-only compatibility shims"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788314634890101001,"uuid":"6780c5ff-88c3-4e74-bf4e-e5e1056263cd"}